    "narrative": "Our offensive ceiling today is anchored by **Corbin Carroll** (87.14), who remains the must-start engine of this lineup. Despite a projected #7 spot in the order, **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a high-upside matchup against M. Adams, with a +14% park adjustment and a +6% dynamic platoon advantage that positions him for explosive production. Similarly, **Mickey Moniak** (75.75) and **James Wood** (74.56) represent our highest-floor outcomes; **Mickey Moniak** thrives on a significant platoon edge against Merrill Kelly, while **James Wood** leverages elite xwOBA metrics and a leadoff spot to capitalize on the favorable matchup against F. Valdez. **Gabriel Moreno** (71.10) continues to be a core contributor as well, as his role at the heart of the order against M. Adams provides consistent value in the counting categories.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the periphery involved **Travis Bazzana** (43.72), who fell just shy of the lineup threshold. While **Travis Bazzana** offers potential, the optimizer favored the higher scoring-floor of **Griffin Conine** (44.05) despite the latter facing a tough matchup against Kevin Gausman. We continue to prioritize our primary depth\u2014including **Vinnie Pasquantino** and **Jose Caballero**\u2014on the bench today, as the current starting configuration provides the best optimization of our limited game caps relative to today\u2019s projected matchups. We remain wary of the \u201cWind In\u201d conditions impacting several of our bats, particularly affecting the raw output projections for **Brice Turang**, **Austin Riley**, **Seiya Suzuki**, and **Griffin Conine**, all of whom carry a -5% wind adjustment that suppresses their scoring potential. Additionally, with many lineups still pending, managers should keep a close eye on the confirmed batting order for **Moises Ballesteros**, **Cole Young**, **Trevor Story**, **Brice Turang**, **Seiya Suzuki**, **Corbin Carroll**, **Griffin Conine**, and **Isaac Paredes** to ensure their positional advantages hold steady as the day progresses. **Tyler Soderstrom** remains on the shelf, leaving us to rely on our active core to maintain our pace in SB and AVG.",
